;; DESIGNED-FLAG DECLARATIONS — per card, per invariant, per theme family.
;;
;; `devcards.invariants/designed-flag-keys` is the shape and the argument. The
;; one thing to know before reading: :kind selects the proof.
;;
;;   :kind :subject         the flag IS what the card exists to render. No
;;                          retiring event exists short of deleting the card, so
;;                          :rationale + :owner and no expiry. The ratchet is the
;;                          STALE clause — an entry matching no finding on a
;;                          family it names is a HARD failure.
;;   :kind :false-positive  the CHECK is wrong about this case. That HAS a
;;                          retiring event, so it owes the full waiver proof
;;                          (:rationale :retires-when :owner :expires) through
;;                          the same `outcome/check-proof!` a waiver runs.
;;
;; Getting that split wrong is the defect this file was reviewed for: the CLASS 1
;; and CLASS 4 entries say in their own rationale that the check is wrong here,
;; and they rode the no-expiry path until :kind was introduced.
;;
;; :families IS THE POINT — CLASS 1, 3 and 4 name only #{1 2}, so a family-0
;; regression on those same cards still reds the gate. Only CLASS 2 names family
;; 0, because a wrap needs no padding to go wrong. There is deliberately no
;; "all families" spelling.
;;
;; WHY A SEPARATE FILE rather than a key on each card in spec.edn: spec.edn does
;; not round-trip through a pretty-printer, so adding a key to 26 cards
;; programmatically would reformat the whole corpus and bury the change. Both
;; corpus lanes — atomic and composition — read this one file, keyed by card id.
{:doc
 "Cards whose subject is a layout-defect flag, or whose flag is an artifact of a
  check that conflates two questions, keyed by card id. Loaded by
  devcards.designed and applied by devcards.invariants/apply-designed-flags."

 :cards
 {  ;; ── CLASS 1 (:false-positive) — the label overruns the button's CONTENT box
  ;; under stock padding while staying inside its COORDS.
  ;;
  ;; Measured on lv_button/default/medium, family 1: button [0 0 79 35], stock
  ;; content box [24 14 55 21] — pad_hor PAD_DEF 24, pad_ver PAD_SMALL 14, so a
  ;; VALID rect and not the inverted case `content_box_inverted` handles — and
  ;; label [24 14 61 31]. The label's x2 61 and y2 31 both pass the content box.
  ;;
  ;; NOTHING IS VISUALLY CLIPPED, verified by eye on the committed vanilla
  ;; renders: "Save" is centred and complete, because LVGL clips a child to the
  ;; parent's COORDS and padding is a layout inset rather than a clip. So the
  ;; check is answering the content-box FIT question under a name that reads as a
  ;; visible clip — which is why these are :false-positive with a retiring event
  ;; rather than a declared subject.
  ;;
  ;; The card cannot author its way out: authoring pad on the widget under test
  ;; defeats the theme fallthrough that IS the object under test. spec.edn's
  ;; unstyled law does permit raw pad-all slots, so it is the fallthrough and not
  ;; the law that forbids it here. Family 0 is enforced and clean at every size.
  "lv_button/default/medium"
  [{:invariant :overflow :node "lv_button" :families #{1 2}
    :kind :false-positive
    :rationale
     "the button's reported scroll extent is the same content-box excess as its
     :clipped entry, seen from the container's side; nothing is drawn outside"
    :retires-when
     "the :clipped / :overflow content-box FIT verdict is split from the
      visible-clip verdict, so a widget whose label overruns a stock-padded
      content box while staying inside its coords stops being reported at all"
    :expires "2026-10-20"
    :owner "jaremko"}
    {:invariant :clipped :node "lv_label" :families #{1 2}
    :kind :false-positive
    :rationale
     "the label overruns the button's stock CONTENT box while staying inside its
     coords, so nothing is drawn outside the button (CLASS 1)"
    :retires-when
     "the :clipped / :overflow content-box FIT verdict is split from the
      visible-clip verdict, so a widget whose label overruns a stock-padded
      content box while staying inside its coords stops being reported at all"
    :expires "2026-10-20"
    :owner "jaremko"}]

