     inertness contract, so it reflows identically"
    :owner "jaremko"}]

  ;; ── CLASS 3 (:subject) — the card IS the padding-floor probe, and under stock
  ;; the chip really is cut off.
  ;;
  ;; Unlike CLASS 1 this one IS visibly clipped, verified on the committed
  ;; vanilla render: the inner chip sits at the bottom-right of its parent with
  ;; its far edges outside it. Measured family 1 — parent [0 0 39 39], chip
  ;; [26 26 45 45], so x2/y2 45 escape the parent's COORDS, not merely its
  ;; content box. The content origin is 26 rather than 24 because a card-styled
  ;; lv_obj adds BORDER_WIDTH 2 to PAD_DEF 24 and `lv_obj_get_style_space_*`
  ;; counts the border.
  ;;
  ;; That is the card's declared purpose: spec.edn's own :sizes note calls :small
  ;; "the RADIUS_DEFAULT=12 + PAD_DEF=24 defect probe". Before this declaration
  ;; the probe's purpose was prose nothing checked; now the corpus asserts the
  ;; probe still probes, which is why it is a :subject and not a concession.
  "lv_obj/default/small"
  [{:invariant :clipped :node "lv_obj" :families #{1 2}
    :kind :subject
    :rationale
     "the declared padding-floor probe: stock's space leaves a 40px box no content
     area, so the 20px chip is drawn past its parent's coords. Visibly clipped,
     and that IS the probe's result"
    :owner "jaremko"}]

  "lv_obj/disabled/small"
  [{:invariant :clipped :node "lv_obj" :families #{1 2}
    :kind :subject
    :rationale
     "the inert twin of lv_obj/default/small, content-identical by the inertness
     contract, so it probes the same floor identically"
    :owner "jaremko"}]

